{
  "_comment": [
    "Provider registry and model catalog. This file is DATA: it is the one place",
    "provider endpoints and wire model ids may appear, and the brand gate",
    "allowlists it for that reason. Delete a provider's entries and the tree has",
    "literal zero occurrences of that provider.",
    "",
    "",
    "env_key names the environment variable holding that provider's key. It is",
    "the provider's own conventional name, not a bcode one, so an existing",
    "key in your shell, under the provider's usual variable name, just works.",
    "context_window is the window bcode will USE, which is not always the window",
    "the provider offers. DeepSeek v4 accepts 1M tokens; we cap at 500k because",
    "quality degrades well before the limit. llama.cpp rows start at 8192 and",
    "are replaced at session start by GET /props n_ctx (never n_ctx_train).",
    "Raise it per model with [model.<id>].context_window if you disagree.",
    "",
    "",
    "Model ids, context windows and output limits are taken from each provider's",
    "own documentation, not from memory. Verified 2026-09-06.",
    "",
    "Prices live in the bcode-pricing crate, not here.",
    "",
    "max_completion_tokens is deliberately unset. A provider's own maximum can",
    "exceed the window we clamp to (DeepSeek allows 384K output against a 1M",
    "window; we cap context at 500k), and sending a cap that large risks",
    "input + max_output exceeding the window. Absent, the provider applies its",
    "own limit, which is what upstream did for its models too.",
    "",
    "",
    "providers is the registry `bcode login` and the provider-scoped credential",
    "tier (auth::accounts::provider_credential) read: one entry per provider,",
    "keyed by id. A model row's provider is its model_family; there is no",
    "separate per-model provider field. A credential stored under this id",
    "(`bcode login`, scope `provider::<id>` in auth.json) works for every model",
    "that shares the model_family, with no config.toml edit."
  ],
  "providers": [
    {
      "id": "deepseek",
      "name": "DeepSeek",
      "base_url": "https://api.deepseek.com/v1",
      "env_key": "DEEPSEEK_API_KEY",
      "default_model": "deepseek-v4-pro",
      "api_key_url": "https://platform.deepseek.com/api_keys"
    },
    {
      "id": "openai",
      "name": "OpenAI",
      "base_url": "https://api.openai.com/v1",
      "env_key": "OPENAI_API_KEY",
      "default_model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
      "api_key_url": "https://platform.openai.com/api-keys",
      "auth": {
        "issuer": "https://auth.openai.com",
        "client_id": "app_EMoamEEZ73f0CkXaXp7hrann",
        "scopes": [
          "openid",
          "profile",
          "email",
          "offline_access",
          "api.connectors.read",
          "api.connectors.invoke"
        ],
        "redirect_ports": [1455, 1457],
        "profile": "chatgpt",
        "authorize_path": "/oauth/authorize",
        "token_path": "/oauth/token",
        "redirect_host": "localhost",
        "redirect_path": "/auth/callback",
        "authorize_extra": {
          "id_token_add_organizations": "true",
          "codex_cli_simplified_flow": "true",
          "originator": "bcode"
        },
        "requested_token": "openai-api-key",
        "json_refresh": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "xai",
      "name": "xAI",
      "base_url": "https://api.x.ai/v1",
      "env_key": "XAI_API_KEY",
      "default_model": "grok-4.6",
      "api_key_url": "https://console.x.ai"
    },
    {
      "id": "llamacpp",
      "name": "llama.cpp",
      "base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1",
      "env_key": "LLAMA_API_KEY",
      "default_model": "llamacpp",
      "api_key_url": "https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/blob/master/tools/server/README.md",
      "probe": "llamacpp"
    }
  ],
